\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Lord and master of us all,
\par Whate'er our name or sign,
\par We own Thy sway, we hear Thy call,
\par We test our lives by Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou judgest us: Thy purity
\par Doth all our lusts condemn;
\par The love that draws us nearer Thee
\par Is hot with wrath to them. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Our thoughts lie open to Thy sight;
\par And, naked to Thy glance,
\par Our secret sins are in the light
\par Of Thy pure countenance.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Yet, weak and blinded though we be,
\par Thou dost our service own,
\par We bring our varying gifts to Thee,
\par And Thou rejectest none.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Apart from Thee all gain is loss,
\par All labour vainly done;
\par The solemn shadow of Thy Cross
\par is better than the sun.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Our Friend, our Brother, and our Lord,
\par What may Thy service be?
\par Nor name, nor form, nor ritual word,
\par But simply following Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. We faintly hear, we dimly see,
\par In differing phrase we pray;
\par But, dim or clear, we own in Thee
\par The Light, the Truth, the Way.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

